time=2026-10-26T23:04:44.776Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-0b95d9fb attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe splitRegions function separates a file's text into the text outside sedum regions and the markers of the regions.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives the file content as a string\n- The function returns three values in order: the text outside regions as a string, a slice of regionMarker, and a boolean that is false when the content is malformed\n- The content is split into lines on the newline character\n- The lines outside regions are rejoined with newline characters in their original order\n- An opening line starts with optional indentation of spaces or tabs\n- An opening line continues with a line-comment leader that is \"//\" or \"#\"\n- An opening line continues with exactly one space\n- An opening line continues with \"sedum:\" followed by an action name of one or more characters without spaces\n- An opening line continues with one space and then a JSON object that extends to the end of the line, trailing whitespace ignored\n- A line whose JSON fails to parse is ordinary text, not malformed\n- A line whose JSON has trailing text after the object is ordinary text\n- A line whose JSON object lacks any of the keys tier, record, gen and pkg is ordinary text\n- A line whose tier, record, gen or pkg value is not a string is ordinary text\n- The JSON object's other keys may hold any value\n- A line of the form \"sedum:anchor:\" and a name with no JSON is ordinary text\n- A closing line starts with optional indentation of spaces or tabs\n- A closing line continues with the same leader as the opening line\n- A closing line continues with exactly one space\n- A closing line continues with \"/sedum:\" followed by the opening line's action name, trailing whitespace ignored\n- The lines between an opening line and its closing line are the region body and are left out of the returned text\n- Each region contributes one placeholder line to the returned text in place of its opening line, body and closing line\n- The placeholder line is the same text for every region and every call; only equality between calls matters\n- A line inside a region that is itself a valid opening line makes the content malformed\n- A region with no closing line before the end of the content makes the content malformed\n- A closing line outside any region is ordinary text\n- Other lines inside a region, including closing lines of a different action, belong to the body\n- On malformed content the function returns an empty string, a nil slice and false\n- On well-formed content the function returns the outside text, the markers and true\n- Content without any region gives an empty marker slice and true\n- For each region the slice holds one regionMarker, in file order\n- Each regionMarker's Tier is the tier string of the opening line's JSON object\n- Each regionMarker's Record is the record string of the opening line's JSON object\n- Each regionMarker's Gen is the gen string of the opening line's JSON object\n- Each regionMarker's Pkg is the pkg string of the opening line's JSON object\n- Each regionMarker's Prefix is the opening line's text before the opening brace of its JSON object, unchanged, with indentation, leader, action name and the following space included\n- Each regionMarker's Body is the text of the lines between the opening and closing lines, each line followed by a newline character\n- A region with no body lines has an empty Body\n- Each regionMarker's Close is the closing line's text unchanged, including any indentation and trailing whitespace\n- An opening line whose JSON object holds a numeric v key is parsed like any other opening line\n- An opening line whose JSON object holds a kwargs key with a string value is parsed like any other opening line\n- regionMarker is the struct declared in regen_run.go with the string fields Tier, Record, Gen, Pkg, Prefix, Body and Close\n- The function adds no imports\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func splitRegions(content string) (string, []regionMarker, bool) {\\n\\tconst placeholder = \\\"// sedum-region\\\"\\n\\tisWS := func(c byte) bool { return c == ' ' || c == '\\\\t' || c == '\\\\r' }\\n\\ttrimRight := func(s string) string {\\n\\t\\tend := len(s)\\n\\t\\tfor end \\u003e 0 \\u0026\\u0026 isWS(s[end-1]) {\\n\\t\\t\\tend--\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn s[:end]\\n\\t}\\n\\tskipWS := func(s string, pos int) int {\\n\\t\\tfor pos \\u003c len(s) \\u0026\\u0026 isWS(s[pos]) {\\n\\t\\t\\tpos++\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn pos\\n\\t}\\n\\tparseString := func(s string, pos int) (string, int, bool) {\\n\\t\\tif pos \\u003e= len(s) || s[pos] != '\\\"' {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", pos, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tvar buf []byte\\n\\t\\ti := pos + 1\\n\\t\\tfor i \\u003c len(s) {\\n\\t\\t\\tc := s[i]\\n\\t\\t\\tif c == '\\\"' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn string(buf), i + 1, true\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif c == '\\\\\\\\' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif i+1 \\u003e= len(s) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", pos, false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\te := s[i+1]\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tswitch e {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcase 'n':\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbuf = append(buf, '\\\\n')\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcase 't':\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbuf = append(buf, '\\\\t')\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcase 'r':\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbuf = append(buf, '\\\\r')\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcase 'b', 'f':\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcase 'u':\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif i+5 \\u003e= len(s) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", pos, false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ti += 4\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbuf = append(buf, e)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ti += 2\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tbuf = append(buf, c)\\n\\t\\t\\ti++\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", pos, false\\n\\t}\\n\\tskipValue := func(s string, pos int) (int, bool) {\\n\\t\\tdepth := 0\\n\\t\\ti := pos\\n\\t\\tfor i \\u003c len(s) {\\n\\t\\t\\tc := s[i]\\n\\t\\t\\tif c == '\\\"' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t_, j, ok := parseString(s, i)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn pos, false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ti = j\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif c == '{' || c == '[' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tdepth++\\n\\t\\t\\t} else if c == '}' || c == ']' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif depth == 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tdepth--\\n\\t\\t\\t} else if c == ',' \\u0026\\u0026 depth == 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\ti++\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif i == pos || depth != 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn pos, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn i, true\\n\\t}\\n\\tparseJSON := func(s string) (map[string]string, bool) {\\n\\t\\tstrs := map[string]string{}\\n\\t\\ti := skipWS(s, 0)\\n\\t\\tif i \\u003e= len(s) || s[i] != '{' {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\ti = skipWS(s, i+1)\\n\\t\\tif i \\u003c len(s) \\u0026\\u0026 s[i] == '}' {\\n\\t\\t\\ti++\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tfor {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tkey, j, ok := parseString(s, i)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ti = skipWS(s, j)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif i \\u003e= len(s) || s[i] != ':' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ti = skipWS(s, i+1)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif i \\u003c len(s) \\u0026\\u0026 s[i] == '\\\"' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tv, j2, ok2 := parseString(s, i)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif !ok2 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tstrs[key] = v\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ti = j2\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tj2, ok2 := skipValue(s, i)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif !ok2 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ti = j2\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ti = skipWS(s, i)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif i \\u003c len(s) \\u0026\\u0026 s[i] == ',' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ti = skipWS(s, i+1)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif i \\u003c len(s) \\u0026\\u0026 s[i] == '}' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ti++\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif skipWS(s, i) != len(s) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn strs, true\\n\\t}\\n\\tparseOpen := func(line string) (string, string, regionMarker, bool) {\\n\\t\\ti := skipWS(line, 0)\\n\\t\\trest := line[i:]\\n\\t\\tvar leader string\\n\\t\\tswitch {\\n\\t\\tcase len(rest) \\u003e= 2 \\u0026\\u0026 rest[0] == '/' \\u0026\\u0026 rest[1] == '/':\\n\\t\\t\\tleader = \\\"//\\\"\\n\\t\\tcase len(rest) \\u003e= 1 \\u0026\\u0026 rest[0] == '#':\\n\\t\\t\\tleader = \\\"#\\\"\\n\\t\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", \\\"\\\", regionMarker{}, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\trest = rest[len(leader):]\\n\\t\\tconst prefix = \\\" sedum:\\\"\\n\\t\\tif len(rest) \\u003c len(prefix) || rest[:len(prefix)] != prefix {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", \\\"\\\", regionMarker{}, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\trest = rest[len(prefix):]\\n\\t\\tsp := -1\\n\\t\\tfor k := 0; k \\u003c len(rest); k++ {\\n\\t\\t\\tif rest[k] == ' ' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tsp = k\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif sp \\u003c= 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", \\\"\\\", regionMarker{}, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\taction := rest[:sp]\\n\\t\\tstrs, ok := parseJSON(trimRight(rest[sp+1:]))\\n\\t\\tif !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", \\\"\\\", regionMarker{}, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\ttier, ok1 := strs[\\\"tier\\\"]\\n\\t\\trecord, ok2 := strs[\\\"record\\\"]\\n\\t\\tgen, ok3 := strs[\\\"gen\\\"]\\n\\t\\t_, ok4 := strs[\\\"pkg\\\"]\\n\\t\\tif !ok1 || !ok2 || !ok3 || !ok4 {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", \\\"\\\", regionMarker{}, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn leader, action, regionMarker{Tier: tier, Record: record, Gen: gen}, true\\n\\t}\\n\\tcloses := func(line, leader, action string) bool {\\n\\t\\ti := skipWS(line, 0)\\n\\t\\trest := line[i:]\\n\\t\\tif len(rest) \\u003c len(leader)+1 || rest[:len(leader)] != leader || rest[len(leader)] != ' ' {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\trest = rest[len(leader)+1:]\\n\\t\\twant := \\\"/sedum:\\\" + action\\n\\t\\tif len(rest) \\u003c len(want) || rest[:len(want)] != want {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn trimRight(rest[len(want):]) == \\\"\\\"\\n\\t}\\n\\tvar lines []string\\n\\tstart := 0\\n\\tfor i := 0; i \\u003c= len(content); i++ {\\n\\t\\tif i == len(content) || content[i] == '\\\\n' {\\n\\t\\t\\tlines = append(lines, content[start:i])\\n\\t\\t\\tstart = i + 1\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tvar out []string\\n\\tmarkers := []regionMarker{}\\n\\tinRegion := false\\n\\tvar leader, action string\\n\\tvar marker regionMarker\\n\\tfor _, line := range lines {\\n\\t\\tif !inRegion {\\n\\t\\t\\tl, a, m, ok := parseOpen(line)\\n\\t\\t\\tif ok {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tinRegion = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tleader, action, marker = l, a, m\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, placeholder)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, line)\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif closes(line, leader, action) {\\n\\t\\t\\tinRegion = false\\n\\t\\t\\tmarkers = append(markers, marker)\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif _, _, _, ok := parseOpen(line); ok {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tif inRegion {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, false\\n\\t}\\n\\tvar buf []byte\\n\\tfor i, l := range out {\\n\\t\\tif i \\u003e 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\tbuf = append(buf, '\\\\n')\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tbuf = append(buf, l...)\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn string(buf), markers, true\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"splitRegions\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-